NAME
       diff - compare files line by line

SYNOPSIS
       diff [-qiw] [-U N] FILE1 FILE2

DESCRIPTION
       Compare two text files and print the differences in unified format:
       lines starting with - are only in FILE1, lines starting with + only in
       FILE2. Colored on a terminal.

OPTIONS
       -q, --brief
           report only whether the files differ

       -i
           ignore case

       -w, -b
           ignore white space

       -U N
           show N lines of context (default 3)

       -u
           unified format (always on)

       --color[=WHEN]
           colorize the output

EXAMPLES
       diff old.c new.c

SEE ALSO
       cmp(1)
